    "reconstruction": {
      "reconstructed_theorem_text": "There exists a single family (mu_n) indexed by all natural numbers n including zero, with each mu_n a genuine Borel probability measure on the real line, having the following three properties simultaneously. For every natural n, let C_n be the finite carrier of all Boolean functions on the indices {0,...,n-1}, let N_n = |C_n| (hence N_n = 2^n), and let U_n = (N_n)^(-1) times counting measure on C_n, where the cardinal and its inverse are taken in the extended nonnegative reals. Define s(true)=1 and s(false)=-1 in the reals and T_n(epsilon) = (sqrt(n))^(-1) times the sum of s(epsilon(j)) over all j<n. The underlying measure of mu_n is exactly the measurable pushforward (T_n)_* U_n. In addition, the underlying measure of mu_0 is the Dirac probability measure at real zero. Finally, as n tends to infinity through the natural numbers, mu_(n+1) converges to the real Gaussian probability measure with mean zero and variance one in the canonical weak topology on real Borel probability measures. Equivalently, for every bounded continuous real test function f, the integrals of f against mu_(n+1) converge to its integral against that Gaussian. The formula defining T_n uses the totalized real inverse, so inverse zero is zero and the empty coordinate sum at n=0 is zero; C_0 consists of its unique empty Boolean configuration and its counting/cardinality law has mass one. The theorem has no caller-supplied premises: the probability-law family, its pushforward identities, its zero-index identity, and its successor-indexed weak convergence are all asserted outputs.",
      "reconstructed_text_sha256": "0ef21c303d8dedd4a39b4b8bae9ed5ca563f8e81ac3e10b3e00a6799264964cc",
      "objects": "One existential family mu: N -> ProbabilityMeasure(R); its underlying Borel measures; the actual finite carriers C_n = (Fin n -> Bool); actual counting measures and their inverse-cardinality normalizations U_n; the literal maps T_n(epsilon) = (sqrt(n))^(-1) * sum_{j in Fin n} (if epsilon(j) then 1 else -1); the real-zero Dirac law; and the genuine real Gaussian law of mean 0 and variance 1. ProbabilityMeasure membership gives total mass 1 for every witness mu_n. Uniform Boolean configurations encode independent symmetric coordinate signs as a consequence of the explicit carrier law, rather than as supplied probabilistic assumptions.",
      "domains": "Indices n range over all natural numbers, including 0. For fixed n, j ranges over Fin n = {0,...,n-1}; epsilon ranges over all Boolean functions on that whole finite index set. Counting/cardinality scaling is in ENNReal; map values, signs, sums, sqrt, and the inverse-sqrt scaling are real. Pushforwards and Dirac measures live on the real Borel space. The variance parameter of gaussianReal is the nonnegative real 1. The family and limit live in the canonical weak topology of ProbabilityMeasure(R); atTop is the natural-number tail filter.",
      "quantifiers": "The outer existential quantifies one complete family mu, shared by all three conjuncts. The first conjunct universally quantifies every n in N and asserts an equality of underlying measures. The epsilon and j variables are locally bound by the pushforward map and finite sum at this same n. The second conjunct specializes the same family at n=0. In the third conjunct the locally bound sequence variable n ranges over N and selects mu_(n+1); Tendsto asserts convergence along every sufficiently large natural-number tail to the fixed Gaussian law. No free variables or quantified caller hypotheses remain. The bounded-continuous-test-function description quantifies arbitrary bounded continuous real test functions only as a semantic equivalent of the stated weak-topology convergence.",
      "assumptions": "None at the theorem boundary: this is a closed proposition. The approved definitions fix the finite measurable structure on C_n, real Borel probabilities and their canonical weak topology, totalized real inversion, literal sign-map semantics, actual measurable pushforward, and the Gaussian mean/variance convention. They do not supply a law family or an independence, moment, central-limit, entropy, regularity, or transport certificate as a premise. The packet compiled flag is not independently checked by this decoder.",
      "conclusion": "There exists a family of genuine probabilities whose underlying measures equal the explicit normalized-counting pushforward for every n >= 0, whose zero member is exactly delta_0, and whose sequence of positive-index members mu_(n+1) tends weakly to N(0,1). All three claims refer to the same existential family. The limit is weak probability-law convergence, not convergence of sampled values, densities, moments, total variation, entropy, or a transport metric; no rate is asserted.",
      "scopes": "The universal n in the first conjunct does not bind the other conjuncts; their zero index and separate successor-indexed lambda are explicit. At n=0 the carrier is a singleton, normalization is inverse 1, sum is empty, and (sqrt(0))^(-1)=0, so the map sends its sole configuration to real zero. For positive n the scale is 1/sqrt(n), multiplying the entire signed sum with true -> +1 and false -> -1. The limit lambda uses n+1 both when selecting the family and, through that family member identity, in its carrier and normalization: its configuration count is 2^(n+1) and its scale is 1/sqrt(n+1). The finite counting normalization uses the actual number of configurations, not n. The limit Gaussian and its mean 0/variance 1 are fixed outside all sequence variables. ProbabilityMeasure weak neighborhoods are used, not an unspecified topology on raw measures.",
      "constant_dependencies": "All objects depend solely on their explicit index n and fixed definitions. Carrier cardinal N_n=2^n and U_n normalization 1/2^n depend on n; T_n depends on n and epsilon, with fixed signs +1 and -1 and real inverse-square-root scaling. The zero Dirac location is fixed at 0. The Gaussian mean is fixed 0 and its variance is fixed 1 (hence standard deviation 1); no n-dependent Gaussian, auxiliary parameter, hidden constant, convergence rate, or caller data occurs. No external theorem or proof body is consulted.",
